Welcome to PIEG (Pieg isn't even GNU) User manual.
-------------------------------------
Beeps program
If you want to use beeps program remember it's not very usable yet, though some songs work.
Here is an example: 2    4    2    4    1    3    1    5, try running it in beeps.

Keyboard layouts
On first boot the setup program picks the keyboard layout (run setup to
open it again).
If your keys type the wrong characters, run keymap to see the layouts in
/INPUTDEV/KEYBOARD and keymap de (or fr, se, uk, dvorak, colemak, us) to
switch. The choice is kept for the next boot. keymap --test lets you type to
check it. AltGr is the right Alt key.

Mouse and touchpad
PS/2 mice and touchpads (laptop touchpads answer as a standard PS/2 mouse) and
USB 2.0 high-speed mice are supported. The pointer is a green ball with an X
and appears when you first move it. Run mouse to check that one was found and
to see its position and buttons. Touchpads that only speak I2C or xHCI/USB 3
are not supported yet, and low-speed USB mice need a companion controller
driver, which does not exist yet.
